Greetings,

I was in the basement where my storage unit is located in the storage room =
and I observed that the door was ajar and propped open providing access to =
the insecure space. This represents a significant failure to protect my bel=
ongings which I have a reasonable expectation of security. I am not sure ho=
w Thorwin Properties can justify putting my belongings at risk and failing =
to abide by RTB regulations.

I received the following message from the Property Manager on January 10, 2=
024.

"Thorwin applied to RTB for the reduction of service for your tenancy. It m=
eans that communal laundry machines and your storage locker will be removed=
 permanently on May 1, 2024, and there will be no alternative provided. RTB=
 will determine the amount of discount to be added to your monthly rent unt=
il the end of current lease only."

I have not received form 8 yet and these photographs strongly indicate that=
 Thorwin Properties is in breach of regulations.

How are you going to be addressing this?

Thank you,
Evan Rosner
